\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Curated positioning against the actual nearby branches, rather than the raw lexical watchlist. The closest technical neighbors solve different tasks: quadratic Beatty decidability studies numeration-definable Beatty relations rather than exact value recurrences \citep  {schaeffer2024,hieronymi2021,baranwal2021}; symbolic linear recurrence and central-set work study words, return words, or IP-set structure rather than the ordered integer value sequence \citep  {durand1998,durand2000,durand2003,bucci2013}; generalized-polynomial work studies definability of recurrence-value sets rather than embeddings of those values into an ordered Beatty subsequence \citep  {adamczewski2022,byszewski2016,byszewski2023}; Skolem--Mahler--Lech theory starts from a pre-existing recurrence and characterizes its zero or intersection sets \citep  {bell2005,derksen2005}. The present paper is therefore narrow by design: it claims a theorem only where the ordered-value problem can be proved directly.}}{3}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:prior-art-matrix}{{2}{3}{Curated positioning against the actual nearby branches, rather than the raw lexical watchlist. The closest technical neighbors solve different tasks: quadratic Beatty decidability studies numeration-definable Beatty relations rather than exact value recurrences \citep {schaeffer2024,hieronymi2021,baranwal2021}; symbolic linear recurrence and central-set work study words, return words, or IP-set structure rather than the ordered integer value sequence \citep {durand1998,durand2000,durand2003,bucci2013}; generalized-polynomial work studies definability of recurrence-value sets rather than embeddings of those values into an ordered Beatty subsequence \citep {adamczewski2022,byszewski2016,byszewski2023}; Skolem--Mahler--Lech theory starts from a pre-existing recurrence and characterizes its zero or intersection sets \citep {bell2005,derksen2005}. The present paper is therefore narrow by design: it claims a theorem only where the ordered-value problem can be proved directly}{figure.5}{}}
\newlabel{fig:prior-art-matrix@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][2][]3}}
